Corridor bundles a Cellpose model ("cyto2_phase_microfluidic_KK1KK2_combi")
trained by the researchers who produced the microfluidic migration data this
tool was written for. That model is redistributed with their work and is not
covered by the MIT licence above.

Cellpose is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause licence, PyTorch under the
BSD 3-Clause licence, and Qt for Python (PySide6) under the LGPL v3.
